# Civic Ledger queue / wizard page lock

Applies to **IT STD Wizard v3** Desk surfaces and any page using `kt_cl_shell` / `kt_cl_components`.

## Mandatory fresh read (before implementing a new CL page)

1. [`B-Components/COMPONENTS.md`](apps/kentender_v1/docs/std-prod-impl/IT-STD-Wizard-v3/B-Components/COMPONENTS.md)
2. Screen pack mock `code.html` + REVISED spec for that screen (e.g. C1-M3)
3. Reference: UI-00 dashboard + UI-01 home

Do **not** invent a third shell or hand-rolled table/filter/strip markup.

**Precedence:** REVISED pack wins on copy/fields/forbidden terms; `code.html` wins on layout geometry when pack is silent. Never ship mock-only labels (`Locked`, `Fix Now`, `Complete Configuration`) when the pack forbids or omits them.

## Compose only

| Concern | Required |
|---------|----------|
| Shell | `cl_shell.enterNative` + `mountContent`; surface registry |
| Toolbar | Context trail only; no search; leaf title in page header |
| Wizard context | `configurationContextStrip(context)` on **every** UI-01/CFG/WF page — **8 cells** (C1-M3 §4) |
| Queue | `filterBar` + `bindFilterBar` + `queueTable` (Rows per page left of pager) |
| UI-01 regions | `nextBestActionPanel` + `configurationStepsGrid` + `handoffPanel` + `stepDetailsDrawer` |

## Pixel fidelity (hard — do not claim done without this)

Frappe/Bootstrap **will** override Tailwind utilities (`h3` color, button borders, grids, `flex-col`). For every new CL surface:

1. Port layout from the screen `code.html`.
2. **Pin** critical layout/color in `kt_cl_code_layout.css` by `data-testid` (same pattern as UI-00 filters / UI-01 next-action).
3. Assert in Playwright via shared helpers (`ktClQueueContract.ts`, `ktClConfigContext.ts`, `ktClUi01LayoutContract.ts`).
4. Touch `kentender_core/hooks.py` + `bench --site kentender.midas.com clear-cache` after CSS/JS edits.
5. Prefer MCP browser screenshot vs mock before marking UX done.

### UI-01 structural pins (non-negotiable)

These failed in production twice. Do **not** regress:

| Pin | Required behavior |
|-----|-------------------|
| Toolbar trail | Dashboard → Tender Configurations → **Tender Configuration Home** (leaf is `SPAN`, not a link) |
| Next Best Action | Desktop: **single row**, CTA `nowrap` on the **right**, title/reason white on `#002244`. Never `flex-col` in `CONFIG_HOME.nextAction` |
| Handoff header | Title + verified icon same row, icon in fixed well, vertically centered |
| Context strip | Exactly **8** cells including Standard Tender Document; pack field labels |
| Forbidden UI | No `Locked`, `Finalize Configuration`, `Publish Tender`, `Complete Configuration` |

Static guard: `kentender_core.tests.test_ui01_layout_css_contract`  
Playwright: `expectUi01StructuralLayout` in `ktClUi01LayoutContract.ts`

## Refresh-safe identity routes (hard)

`frappe.route_options` and bare query strings **do not survive refresh**.

- Put durable IDs in the **route segment**: `frappe.set_route("it-tender-configuration-overview", configurationId)` → `/desk/.../overview/<id>`.
- On load, accept `route[1]` / `route_options` / query, then **rewrite** to the segment URL.
- Playwright must include a **reload** case that still shows the loaded entity (not the empty-state picker).

## Disallowed

- Hand-rolled context strips / tables / filter bars
- Relying only on `route_options` for page identity
- Shipping CL UI that depends on unpinned Tailwind without layout CSS guards
- Black Desk button chrome on CL action links
- Claiming pixel-faithful without screenshot/Playwright layout evidence
- Adding `flex-col` / wrapping next-action without updating the structural gate

## Regression gates (required before UX "done")

```bash
make -C apps/kentender_v1 ui-civic-ledger-queue-gate
make -C apps/kentender_v1 ui-civic-ledger-ui01-gate
make -C apps/kentender_v1 ui-civic-ledger-cfg01-gate
make -C apps/kentender_v1 ui-civic-ledger-cfg02-gate
make -C apps/kentender_v1 ui-civic-ledger-cfg03-gate
make -C apps/kentender_v1 ui-civic-ledger-cfg04-gate
```

- Queue: `kt-cl-queue-pattern-lock.spec.ts`
- UI-01: `ui01-layout-contract.spec.ts` + `ui01-home.spec.ts` (+ mockups `ui01-mockup-states.spec.ts` when seeding visual states)
- CFG-01: `cfg01-tender-profile.spec.ts` (strip, 8/4 layout, lot table, Save success alert, Back-left footer, high-contrast Continue, refresh-safe ID)
- CFG-02: `cfg02-tender-data-sheet.spec.ts` (strip, 7 groups + sticky guidance, conditional fields, Save / Run Check / Continue, refresh-safe ID)
- CFG-03: `cfg03-it-requirements.spec.ts` (strip, requirements table + drawer, sticky guidance, Save / Run Check / Continue, refresh-safe ID)
- CFG-04: `cfg04-implementation-schedule.spec.ts` (approach toggle, milestones table + drawer / single form, Acceptance Method + Setup Status, drawer persist)
- Wizard footers: compose `wizardStepFooter` — Back left; optional `extraEndActions` (e.g. Run Check); primary Continue uses **white** on `#002244` (not muted on-primary-container)
- Step/overall progress: `step_progress.py` exit-condition checklists (`STEP_CONDITION_BUILDERS`); CFG-01…CFG-04 live; overall % = average of nine step percents — never decorative defaults (e.g. 67%)
- Helpers: `ktClQueueContract.ts`, `ktClConfigContext.ts`, `ktClUi01LayoutContract.ts`

